{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Import necessary libraries"],"metadata":{"id":"C45J_-lKmtDt"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from scipy.odr import ODR, Model, Data"],"metadata":{"id":"Xu8dj_FGmcBG","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428439605,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":71,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}}},"execution_count":5,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 1: Introduction to Line Fitting**\n","\n","\n","    In data analysis, we often want to find a line that best represents a set of data points.\n","    This is called 'line fitting' or 'linear regression'. The goal is to model the relationship\n","    between two variables, typically denoted as x (independent) and y (dependent).\n","\n","    The line is represented by the equation: y = mx + c\n","        - 'm' is the slope of the line.\n","        - 'c' is the y-intercept.\n","\n","    The challenge is to find the optimal 'm' and 'c' that make the line 'best' fit the data.\n","    But what does 'best' mean? This is where different methods like OLS and TLS come in.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"K8ALNrYjmcJv"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Let's create some synthetic data to work with\n","\n","    We'll create data that follows a line and add some noise"],"metadata":{"id":"fnkiEOMVnkc8"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["np.random.seed(42) # for reproducibility\n","true_m = 0.5\n","true_c = 2\n","x_data = np.linspace(0, 10, 20)\n","y_perfect = true_m * x_data + true_c"],"metadata":{"id":"RFXS0EHRmcVI","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428439605,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}}},"execution_count":6,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Add noise only to the y-values (a key assumption for OLS)"],"metadata":{"id":"6HMr8k0Lmch5"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["y_data = y_perfect + np.random.normal(0, 0.75, len(x_data))"],"metadata":{"id":"KkOFCXX5mcxA","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428439606,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":4,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}}},"execution_count":7,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Plot the data"],"metadata":{"id":"OyNBeWb5mc82"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","plt.scatter(x_data, y_data, color='blue', label='Noisy Data Points')\n","plt.plot(x_data, y_perfect, color='red', linestyle='--', label='True Underlying Line')\n","plt.title('Synthetic Data for Line Fitting')\n","plt.xlabel('x')\n","plt.ylabel('y')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":564},"id":"0MFSqSA8mdIt","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428439778,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":175,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"ca71edd2-8a49-46bd-e96a-2998ca46ee6c"},"execution_count":8,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 2: Ordinary Least Squares (OLS)**\n","\n","    Definition:\n","      Ordinary Least Squares is the most common method for linear regression.\n","      Its goal is to find the line that minimizes the sum of the squared *vertical distances*\n","      from each data point to the line. These vertical distances are called 'residuals'.\n","\n","    Assumption:\n","      The key assumption of OLS is that all errors are in the 'y' variable (the dependent variable),\n","      and the 'x' variable is known precisely.\n","\n","    Formulas:\n","        Given n data points (x_i, y_i):\n","        The slope 'm' and intercept 'c' are calculated as follows:\n","\n","            m = Σ [ (x_i - x̄)(y_i - ȳ) ] / Σ [ (x_i - x̄)² ]\n","            c = ȳ - m * x̄\n","\n","              where:\n","              - x̄ is the mean of x values\n","              - ȳ is the mean of y values\n","              - Σ represents the sum over all data points."],"metadata":{"id":"2nUxyseOmdZJ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def ordinary_least_squares(x, y):\n","    \"\"\"Calculates the slope (m) and intercept (c) for OLS.\"\"\"\n","    x_mean = np.mean(x)\n","    y_mean = np.mean(y)\n","\n","    numerator = np.sum((x - x_mean) * (y - y_mean))\n","    denominator = np.sum((x - x_mean)**2)\n","\n","    m = numerator / denominator\n","    c = y_mean - m * x_mean\n","    return m, c\n","\n","# Calculate OLS line for our data\n","m_ols, c_ols = ordinary_least_squares(x_data, y_data)\n","y_ols_fit = m_ols * x_data + c_ols\n","\n","from sklearn.metrics import r2_score\n","# Calculate R² score\n","r2 = r2_score(y_data, y_ols_fit)\n","\n","# Print results\n","print(f\"OLS Calculated Slope (m): {m_ols:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"OLS Calculated Intercept (c): {c_ols:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"R² Score: {r2:.4f}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"GtMn41Hhmdnc","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428439793,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":14,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"41ee92d4-dd90-4d8f-9482-0d59a4104d3b"},"execution_count":9,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["OLS Calculated Slope (m): 0.3581\n","OLS Calculated Intercept (c): 2.5809\n","R² Score: 0.7937\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Visualize OLS"],"metadata":{"id":"G3S0sH3Umdxi"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n","plt.scatter(x_data, y_data, color='blue', label='Data Points')\n","plt.plot(x_data, y_perfect, color='red', linestyle='--', label='True Line')\n","plt.plot(x_data, y_ols_fit, color='green', label=f'OLS Fit: y={m_ols:.2f}x+{c_ols:.2f}\\nR²={r2:.3f}')\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X Values')\n","plt.ylabel('Y Values')\n","plt.title('OLS Line Fitting with R² Score')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":718},"id":"Jaxh2OiEmd7R","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428440045,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":250,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"0896da65-4263-4ab6-a88c-c7cb72b1796f"},"execution_count":10,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Show the vertical errors that OLS minimizes"],"metadata":{"id":"H0ZW68i1meEM"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["for i in range(len(x_data)):\n","    plt.plot([x_data[i], x_data[i]], [y_data[i], y_ols_fit[i]], color='gray', linestyle='--')\n","plt.plot([], [], color='gray', linestyle='--', label='Vertical Errors (Residuals)') # for legend\n","\n","plt.title('Ordinary Least Squares (OLS) Visualization')\n","plt.xlabel('x (Assumed to be error-free)')\n","plt.ylabel('y (Contains errors)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"b0wp2tsCmeOH","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428440354,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":307,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"e3cacdd9-3279-4066-91e7-ee8c26e3b170"},"execution_count":11,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 3: Total Least Squares (TLS)**\n","\n","    Definition:\n","        Total Least Squares (also known as Orthogonal Distance Regression) is a more general method.\n","        It is used when there are measurement errors in *both* the 'x' and 'y' variables.\n","        Instead of minimizing vertical distances, TLS finds the line that minimizes the sum of the\n","        squared orthogonal (perpendicular) distances from each data point to the line.\n","\n","    Method (using Singular Value Decomposition - SVD):\n","        TLS doesn't have simple formulas like OLS. A common way to solve it is using SVD, a powerful\n","        matrix decomposition technique. The steps are:\n","        1. Center the data by subtracting the mean from each x and y point.\n","        2. Form a data matrix 'A' with the centered x and y columns.\n","        3. Compute the SVD of 'A': A = UΣVᵀ\n","        4. The direction of the line is given by the last column of Vᵀ (or V).\n","          This vector, [a, b], defines the line's normal.\n","        5. The line equation is ax + by = 0 for the centered data.\n","          In the form y = mx + c, the slope is m = -a/b.\n","        6. The intercept 'c' is calculated using the original means."],"metadata":{"id":"a3p0TGA4meW3"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["def total_least_squares(x, y):\n","    \"\"\"Calculates the slope (m) and intercept (c) for TLS using SVD.\"\"\"\n","    x_mean = np.mean(x)\n","    y_mean = np.mean(y)\n","\n","    # 1. Center the data\n","    x_centered = x - x_mean\n","    y_centered = y - y_mean\n","\n","    # 2. Form the data matrix\n","    A = np.vstack([x_centered, y_centered]).T\n","\n","    # 3. Compute SVD\n","    U, S, Vt = np.linalg.svd(A)\n","\n","    # 4. Get the direction vector (last column of V or last row of Vt)\n","    # This vector is normal to the line\n","    a, b = Vt[-1, :]\n","\n","    # 5. Calculate the slope\n","    # The line is ax + by = 0 -> y = (-a/b)x\n","    m = -a / b\n","\n","    # 6. Calculate the intercept\n","    # The line must pass through the mean point (x̄, ȳ)\n","    # ȳ = m * x̄ + c => c = ȳ - m * x̄\n","    c = y_mean - m * x_mean\n","    return m, c"],"metadata":{"id":"ZHxLXz_ZmegD","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428440372,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":19,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}}},"execution_count":12,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Let's create new data with errors in BOTH x and y to see TLS shine"],"metadata":{"id":"kuXUfMI2mepR"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["x_data_noisy = x_data + np.random.normal(0, 0.75, len(x_data))\n","y_data_noisy = y_perfect + np.random.normal(0, 0.75, len(x_data))\n","\n","# Calculate TLS line\n","m_tls, c_tls = total_least_squares(x_data_noisy, y_data_noisy)\n","y_tls_fit = m_tls * x_data_noisy + c_tls\n","\n","# Calculate R² score\n","r2_tls = r2_score(y_data_noisy, y_tls_fit)\n","\n","# Print results\n","print(f\"TLS Calculated Slope (m): {m_tls:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"TLS Calculated Intercept (c): {c_tls:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"R² Score: {r2_tls:.4f}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"y740Omodme14","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428597065,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":47,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"38f6e1ab-68d8-450c-949f-b15498b40b83"},"execution_count":21,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["TLS Calculated Slope (m): 0.5478\n","TLS Calculated Intercept (c): 1.8611\n","R² Score: 0.7214\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Visualize TLS"],"metadata":{"id":"XnS4IJHmp79U"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n","plt.scatter(x_data_noisy, y_data_noisy, color='blue', label='Data Points (Errors in X and Y)')\n","plt.plot(x_data, y_perfect, color='red', linestyle='--', label='True Line')\n","plt.plot(x_data_noisy, y_tls_fit, color='purple', label=f'TLS Fit: y={m_tls:.2f}x+{c_tls:.2f}\\nR²={r2_tls:.3f}')\n","\n","plt.xlabel('X Values')\n","plt.ylabel('Y Values')\n","plt.title('Total Least Squares Line Fitting with R² Score')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":718},"id":"6vl379q2p8P-","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428598919,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":208,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"8b8402d8-ed55-4328-c9ff-dd4520428eec"},"execution_count":22,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Show the orthogonal errors that TLS minimizes"],"metadata":{"id":"nyRiSxqQp8aS"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["for i in range(len(x_data_noisy)):\n","    x_point = x_data_noisy[i]\n","    y_point = y_data_noisy[i]\n","    # Find the closest point on the line\n","    x_line = (x_point + m_tls * (y_point - c_tls)) / (1 + m_tls**2)\n","    y_line = m_tls * x_line + c_tls\n","    plt.plot([x_point, x_line], [y_point, y_line], color='gray', linestyle='--')\n","plt.plot([], [], color='gray', linestyle='--', label='Orthogonal Errors') # for legend\n","\n","plt.title('Total Least Squares (TLS) Visualization')\n","plt.xlabel('x (Contains errors)')\n","plt.ylabel('y (Contains errors)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.axis('equal') # Use equal aspect ratio to see orthogonality clearly\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"loFA__8Xp8kL","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428440788,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":217,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"664eccc4-a96f-4dc0-a057-511d2352c1d3"},"execution_count":15,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 4: Real-World Example & Comparison**\n","\n","    Let's use a real-world example. We'll examine the relationship between the\n","    bill length and flipper length of penguins from the Palmer Penguins dataset.\n","    It's reasonable to assume that measuring both could involve some error.\n","\n","    Data Source: Gorman, KB, Williams, TD, Fraser, WR (2014) Ecological Sexual\n","    Dimorphism and Environmental Variability within a Community of Antarctic Penguins\n","    (Genus Pygoscelis). PLoS ONE 9(3): e90081.\n","\n","    We'll use a simplified version of this dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"ojnEgSRWp8tH"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Sample data representing bill length and flipper length (in mm) for Gentoo penguins\n","\n","    In a real scenario, you'd load this from a file (e.g., CSV)"],"metadata":{"id":"5DOt2N4-qlkU"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["bill_length = np.array([46.1, 50.0, 48.7, 50.0, 47.6, 46.5, 45.2, 49.1, 48.4, 50.2, 45.1, 46.5, 50.9, 45.5, 48.2, 55.1, 45.8])\n","flipper_length = np.array([215, 220, 220, 225, 215, 215, 215, 220, 215, 228, 212, 210, 218, 210, 215, 230, 215])\n","\n","# Let's perform both OLS and TLS on this data\n","# OLS: Assumes flipper length is perfect, error is in bill length\n","m_ols_peng, c_ols_peng = ordinary_least_squares(flipper_length, bill_length)\n","# TLS: Assumes both measurements have errors\n","m_tls_peng, c_tls_peng = total_least_squares(flipper_length, bill_length)\n","\n","\n","print(f\"Penguin Data - OLS Slope: {m_ols_peng:.4f}, Intercept: {c_ols_peng:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Penguin Data - TLS Slope: {m_tls_peng:.4f}, Intercept: {c_tls_peng:.4f}\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"kJYhkwlxp825","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428889623,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":8,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"c6941e32-4af5-4d65-899e-78889175baaa"},"execution_count":23,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Penguin Data - OLS Slope: 0.3865, Intercept: -35.9053\n","Penguin Data - TLS Slope: 0.4063, Intercept: -40.2094\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Generate the line data for plotting"],"metadata":{"id":"29IbypPEp8_d"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["x_range_peng = np.linspace(flipper_length.min(), flipper_length.max(), 100)\n","y_ols_peng_fit = m_ols_peng * x_range_peng + c_ols_peng\n","y_tls_peng_fit = m_tls_peng * x_range_peng + c_tls_peng\n","\n","# R² scores\n","y_ols_pred = m_ols_peng * flipper_length + c_ols_peng\n","y_tls_pred = m_tls_peng * flipper_length + c_tls_peng\n","r2_ols = r2_score(bill_length, y_ols_pred)\n","r2_tls = r2_score(bill_length, y_tls_pred)"],"metadata":{"id":"HACT13Gsp9JK","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428891809,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":9,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}}},"execution_count":24,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Plot the comparison"],"metadata":{"id":"GEWu2iGCp9Sf"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n","plt.scatter(flipper_length, bill_length, label='Penguin Data', color='black', zorder=5)\n","plt.plot(x_range_peng, y_ols_peng_fit, color='green',\n","         label=f'OLS Fit: y={m_ols_peng:.2f}x+{c_ols_peng:.2f}\\nR²={r2_ols:.3f}')\n","plt.plot(x_range_peng, y_tls_peng_fit, color='purple',\n","         label=f'TLS Fit: y={m_tls_peng:.2f}x+{c_tls_peng:.2f}\\nR²={r2_tls:.3f}')\n","\n","plt.title('Real-World Example: OLS vs. TLS for Penguin Measurements')\n","plt.xlabel('Flipper Length (mm)')\n","plt.ylabel('Bill Length (mm)')\n","plt.legend()\n","plt.grid(True)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":718},"id":"pavwyNaHp9ci","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428896509,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":247,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"2350b45c-476e-4510-ae0a-06389063a6fd"},"execution_count":25,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Comparison and Conclusion:\n","\n","      - Look at the final plot. The OLS and TLS lines are very similar but not identical.\n","      - OLS minimizes vertical distance, which can \"flatten\" the slope if there's significant error in the x-variable.\n","      - TLS accounts for errors in both x and y, often providing a more physically realistic fit when both measurements are uncertain. In our penguin example, the TLS line has a slightly steeper slope.\n","\n","When to use which?\n","\n","      - Use OLS when you are confident your independent variable (x-axis) is measured with very high precision compared to your dependent variable (y-axis). This is common in controlled experiments.\n","      - Use TLS when both variables are outcomes of measurements and are subject to error. This is common in biology, astronomy, and economics.\n","\n","For the penguin data, TLS is arguably the more appropriate model because both flipper and bill length are physical measurements prone to some level of error."],"metadata":{"id":"tLJ7y0xVrBaY"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 5: Application on a Real Image from the Web**\n","\n","\n","    Now, let's apply these techniques to a real-world image from the web.\n","    We will load an image containing a distinct line, process it, and try to fit a line to it.\n","\n","    This is more challenging than a synthetic image because real images have complex textures,\n","    lighting variations, and perspective distortion.\n","\n","    Steps:\n","    1. Load an image from a URL.\n","    2. Convert the image to grayscale for easier processing.\n","    3. Use an edge detector (Canny edge detection) to find the pixels that form the line.\n","    4. Extract the (x, y) coordinates of the detected edge pixels.\n","    5. Fit lines to these coordinates using both OLS and TLS.\n","    6. Visualize and compare the results on the original image."],"metadata":{"id":"UJVN6LIwrBtT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from skimage import io, color\n","from skimage.feature import canny\n","from skimage.transform import resize\n","import gdown\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Download image from Google Drive using gdown\n","# ===============================\n","file_id = '1ZbkCQ_Fc8EUwEcJKKvzlNMJQR3-GLiCh'  # Replace with your file ID\n","url = f'https://drive.google.com/uc?id={file_id}'\n","output = 'image.jpg'\n","gdown.download(url, output, quiet=False)\n","\n","# Load image\n","image_rgb = io.imread(output)\n","\n","# Validate image shape\n","print(f\"Original image shape: {image_rgb.shape}\")\n","if len(image_rgb.shape) < 2:\n","    raise ValueError(\"Invalid image loaded (maybe an HTML file). Check your Google Drive link.\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Resize image if it's too large\n","# ===============================\n","max_dim = 800  # Max dimension size for safe processing\n","if max(image_rgb.shape[:2]) > max_dim:\n","    scale = max_dim / max(image_rgb.shape[:2])\n","    image_rgb = resize(image_rgb, (int(image_rgb.shape[0] * scale), int(image_rgb.shape[1] * scale)), anti_aliasing=True)\n","    print(f\"Resized image shape: {image_rgb.shape}\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Convert to grayscale\n","# ===============================\n","image_gray = color.rgb2gray(image_rgb)\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Apply Canny edge detection\n","# ===============================\n","edges = canny(image_gray, sigma=1.5)\n","y_coords, x_coords = np.where(edges)\n","\n","print(f\"Total edge points detected: {len(x_coords)}\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Limit number of points for SVD (avoid memory crash)\n","# ===============================\n","max_points = 50000\n","if len(x_coords) > max_points:\n","    idx = np.random.choice(len(x_coords), max_points, replace=False)\n","    x_coords = x_coords[idx]\n","    y_coords = y_coords[idx]\n","    print(f\"Using {max_points} random edge points for fitting.\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Define OLS and TLS functions\n","# ===============================\n","def ordinary_least_squares(x, y):\n","    A = np.vstack([x, np.ones(len(x))]).T\n","    m, c = np.linalg.lstsq(A, y, rcond=None)[0]\n","    return m, c\n","\n","def total_least_squares(x, y):\n","    x_mean, y_mean = np.mean(x), np.mean(y)\n","    x_centered, y_centered = x - x_mean, y - y_mean\n","    A = np.vstack([x_centered, y_centered]).T\n","    _, _, Vt = np.linalg.svd(A, full_matrices=False)\n","    v = Vt[-1, :]\n","    m = -v[0] / v[1]\n","    c = y_mean - m * x_mean\n","    return m, c\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Fit lines using OLS and TLS\n","# ===============================\n","# ===============================\n","# Fit lines using OLS and TLS\n","# ===============================\n","m_ols_img, c_ols_img = ordinary_least_squares(x_coords, y_coords)\n","\n","# For TLS, use smaller subset\n","max_points_tls = 5000\n","if len(x_coords) > max_points_tls:\n","    idx = np.random.choice(len(x_coords), max_points_tls, replace=False)\n","    x_tls = x_coords[idx]\n","    y_tls = y_coords[idx]\n","    print(f\"TLS will use {max_points_tls} random points.\")\n","else:\n","    x_tls = x_coords\n","    y_tls = y_coords\n","\n","try:\n","    m_tls_img, c_tls_img = total_least_squares(x_tls, y_tls)\n","except Exception as e:\n","    print(f\"TLS failed: {e}\")\n","    m_tls_img, c_tls_img = None, None\n","\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Visualization\n","# ===============================\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(20, 7))\n","ax = axes.ravel()\n","\n","# Original Image\n","ax[0].imshow(image_rgb)\n","ax[0].set_title('Original Image')\n","ax[0].axis('off')\n","\n","# Edge Image\n","ax[1].imshow(edges, cmap=plt.cm.gray)\n","ax[1].set_title('Canny Edge Detection')\n","ax[1].axis('off')\n","\n","# Fitted Lines\n","ax[2].imshow(image_rgb)\n","x_range_img = np.array([0, image_rgb.shape[1]])\n","y_ols_img_fit = m_ols_img * x_range_img + c_ols_img\n","y_tls_img_fit = m_tls_img * x_range_img + c_tls_img\n","\n","ax[2].plot(x_range_img, y_ols_img_fit, color='lime', linewidth=3, label='OLS Fit')\n","ax[2].plot(x_range_img, y_tls_img_fit, color='cyan', linewidth=3, label='TLS Fit')\n","ax[2].set_title('OLS vs TLS Fit')\n","ax[2].set_xlim(0, image_rgb.shape[1])\n","ax[2].set_ylim(image_rgb.shape[0], 0)\n","ax[2].legend()\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n","\n","print(\"\"\"\n","Image Fitting Summary:\n","- Resized large images to prevent memory crashes.\n","- Limited edge points to 50,000 for stable SVD computation.\n","- Used gdown for robust Google Drive download.\n","- OLS minimizes vertical error, TLS minimizes perpendicular error.\n","\"\"\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":719},"id":"QkRGSd-irB6b","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428444580,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":3529,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"0ece0d7e-4199-4bca-f8f1-3e4cc17dc434"},"execution_count":19,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["Downloading...\n","From: https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1ZbkCQ_Fc8EUwEcJKKvzlNMJQR3-GLiCh\n","To: /content/image.jpg\n","100%|██████████| 203k/203k [00:00<00:00, 83.6MB/s]\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Original image shape: (1143, 1222, 3)\n","Resized image shape: (748, 800, 3)\n","Total edge points detected: 36861\n","TLS will use 5000 random points.\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 2000x700 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","Image Fitting Summary:\n","- Resized large images to prevent memory crashes.\n","- Limited edge points to 50,000 for stable SVD computation.\n","- Used gdown for robust Google Drive download.\n","- OLS minimizes vertical error, TLS minimizes perpendicular error.\n","\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Note to Students:**\n","\n","    As you can see from the previous results, OLS and TLS did not give good results.\n","\n","    This is because these methods try to fit a single line to all the detected edge points, which fails in our case since the Sudoku image contains multiple grid lines, intersections, and noise from digits.\n","\n","    To handle this, we will now proceed with Hough Transform (which can detect multiple straight lines) and RANSAC (which robustly fits a dominant line by ignoring outliers) for the same image."],"metadata":{"id":"wFYT_1-W3Zy9"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Section 6: Application of RANSAC (Robust Line Fitting) and Hough Transform for the same Real Image from the Web**"],"metadata":{"id":"owRTYFthrCGU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["1. Hough Transform\n","\n","        Definition: A feature extraction technique that detects straight lines in an image by transforming edge points from Cartesian space (x,y) into parameter space (ρ,θ).\n","\n","        Line equation in Hough space:\n","        ρ=xcosθ+ysinθ\n","          where:\n","            ρ = distance from the origin to the line,\n","            θ = angle of the normal vector.\n","\n","        How it works:\n","\n","        Each edge point votes for all possible lines passing through it.\n","        The most voted lines are considered as detected lines.\n","\n","2. RANSAC (Random Sample Consensus)\n","\n","        Definition: A robust regression method that fits a model to data containing outliers by iteratively selecting random subsets.\n","\n","        Line equation:\n","          y=mx+c\n","            where:\n","              m = slope,\n","              c = intercept.\n","\n","        Algorithm steps:\n","            Randomly sample a small subset of points.\n","            Fit a model (line) to this subset.\n","            Count how many points from the entire dataset fit this model within a tolerance (inliers)."],"metadata":{"id":"P9sZet4P0VhF"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from skimage import io, color\n","from skimage.feature import canny\n","from skimage.transform import resize, probabilistic_hough_line\n","from sklearn.linear_model import RANSACRegressor\n","import gdown\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Step 1: Download image from Google Drive\n","# ===============================\n","file_id = '1ZbkCQ_Fc8EUwEcJKKvzlNMJQR3-GLiCh'  # Replace if needed\n","url = f'https://drive.google.com/uc?id={file_id}'\n","output = 'image.jpg'\n","gdown.download(url, output, quiet=False)\n","\n","# Load image\n","image_rgb = io.imread(output)\n","print(f\"Original image shape: {image_rgb.shape}\")\n","\n","# Resize to prevent memory overload\n","max_dim = 800\n","if max(image_rgb.shape[:2]) > max_dim:\n","    scale = max_dim / max(image_rgb.shape[:2])\n","    image_rgb = resize(image_rgb, (int(image_rgb.shape[0]*scale), int(image_rgb.shape[1]*scale)), anti_aliasing=True)\n","    print(f\"Resized image shape: {image_rgb.shape}\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Step 2: Convert to grayscale and detect edges\n","# ===============================\n","image_gray = color.rgb2gray(image_rgb)\n","edges = canny(image_gray, sigma=2)\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Step 3: Hough Transform for multiple lines\n","# ===============================\n","lines = probabilistic_hough_line(edges, threshold=10, line_length=50, line_gap=3)\n","print(f\"Detected {len(lines)} lines with Hough Transform\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Step 4: RANSAC for best line (optional)\n","# ===============================\n","# Flatten edge coordinates\n","y_coords, x_coords = np.where(edges)\n","X = x_coords.reshape(-1, 1)\n","y = y_coords\n","\n","# Fit RANSAC model\n","ransac = RANSACRegressor(residual_threshold=2, max_trials=100)\n","ransac.fit(X, y)\n","m_ransac = ransac.estimator_.coef_[0]\n","c_ransac = ransac.estimator_.intercept_\n","print(f\"RANSAC Line: slope={m_ransac:.4f}, intercept={c_ransac:.4f}\")\n","\n","# ===============================\n","# Step 5: Visualization\n","# ===============================\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(22, 8))\n","ax = axes.ravel()\n","\n","# Original image\n","ax[0].imshow(image_rgb)\n","ax[0].set_title(\"Original Image\")\n","ax[0].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","# Edge detection\n","ax[1].imshow(edges, cmap=plt.cm.gray)\n","ax[1].set_title(\"Canny Edge Detection\")\n","ax[1].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","# Hough + RANSAC Lines\n","ax[2].imshow(image_rgb)\n","for line in lines:\n","    p0, p1 = line\n","    ax[2].plot((p0[0], p1[0]), (p0[1], p1[1]), color='yellow', linewidth=2)\n","\n","# Add RANSAC line\n","x_range = np.array([0, image_rgb.shape[1]])\n","y_ransac_fit = m_ransac * x_range + c_ransac\n","ax[2].plot(x_range, y_ransac_fit, color='cyan', linewidth=3, label='RANSAC Fit')\n","\n","ax[2].set_title(\"Hough Lines + RANSAC Line\")\n","ax[2].axis(\"off\")\n","ax[2].legend()\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":594},"id":"H_nDt6U1rCQY","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1757428448477,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":3892,"user":{"displayName":"AYAN PAUL","userId":"11246289557973384086"}},"outputId":"0deb1b6b-2e3c-4171-d76b-308faf6091f0"},"execution_count":20,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["Downloading...\n","From: https://drive.google.com/uc?id=1ZbkCQ_Fc8EUwEcJKKvzlNMJQR3-GLiCh\n","To: /content/image.jpg\n","100%|██████████| 203k/203k [00:00<00:00, 57.6MB/s]\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Original image shape: (1143, 1222, 3)\n","Resized image shape: (748, 800, 3)\n","Detected 294 lines with Hough Transform\n","RANSAC Line: slope=0.3510, intercept=214.8432\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 2200x800 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["        ✔ OLS and TLS FAILED because they tried to fit one line for all points.\n","        ✔ Hough → detects all straight grid lines, giving full Sudoku structure.\n","        ✔ RANSAC → fits the dominant line robustly, ignoring noise and outliers.\n","        ✔ Handles rotated grids and 